{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And as for what is written, <b>\"I am the Elohim of your father\"</b> — our Rabbis of blessed memory explained (Exodus Rabbah 3:1) that the Holy One, blessed be He, appeared to him in the voice of Amram his father, and when he said 'Here I am,' the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: 'This is not the voice of your father, but the voice of the Elohei of your father Amram.' And the word \"Elohim\" is written here four times, corresponding to the four expressions of redemption, as will be explained with the help of YHWH in the portion of Va'era (Exodus 6:6). And there are those who explain that the reason He mentioned 'the Elohei of your father' is because He thereby revealed to him that his father had already died — once He had singled out His name, blessed be He, upon him — and so that he would not refuse to go on this mission in his father's place, for even before Aaron his older brother he would have refused to take on this authority — how much the more so in his father's place."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:18:02.747132347Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}